  "description": "KAMNIY crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H90 N8 O26 Tb6. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb1B (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2B (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3B (Tb) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.485-3.858 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.03-118.71°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C96H90Tb6N8O26. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
